# Cursor rules — Ratul's portfolio (multi-agent repo)

You share this repo with another AI agent, Claude Code, which owns the
data/platform lane. The full lane map + protocol lives in `AGENTS.md` (repo
root) — read it. Summary, as HARD constraints:

## Your lane (you may edit)
- `portfolio-site/app/**` — public pages, layout, UI components
  (`app/components/**`), hooks (`app/hooks/**`), styles
  — EXCEPT the Claude-owned carve-outs below.

## NEVER edit (Claude's lane)
- `portfolio-site/lib/**`          (data layer / content API — consume read-only)
- `portfolio-site/supabase/**`     (schema, migrations, RLS)
- `portfolio-site/app/api/**`      (route handlers)
- `portfolio-site/app/capture/**`  (admin/capture surfaces)
- `portfolio-site/scripts/**`
- `docs/claude-planning/**`        (planning docs + progress log)
- `docs/assessment/**`             (historical, read-only)
- `.claude/**`

## The shared contract
`portfolio-site/lib/content/types.ts` is the agreed interface. Import from
`@/lib/content` only. If you need a new field/shape: STOP, tell Ratul what you
need and why — do NOT edit the contract, define parallel local types, or work
around it. Claude extends the contract, then you build on it.

## Protocol
- If a task requires touching a NEVER-edit path: stop and tell Ratul exactly
  what you need from Claude instead.
- Commit small and often. Shared config edits (`package.json`,
  `next.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, …) require an explicit
  `chore(config): …` commit-message callout.
- No destructive git (`reset --hard`, `checkout -- <file>`, force-push) —
  uncommitted work may belong to the other agent.
- Before building on `lib/content` data, re-read the current exports — Claude
  may have extended the contract since your last read.
